        "task": "White-box BOLA/IDOR discovery sweep over /workspace/server/src/routes/*.ts (Express 5 + Prisma; call get_threat_model target /workspace/server first).\n\nSHELL QUIRK: exec_command default pipes swallow output — always pass tty:true.\n\nCONTEXT: Multi-tenant by `Patient.ownerId`. `requireAuth` only authenticates (injects req.userId); object scoping is per-handler. Helpers exist: `userPatientIds(userId)`, `firstPatientId(userId)`. Exams/items/analyses etc. link to patientId (or userId directly). CUID ids are non-enumerable but secrecy is not authorization.\n\nYOUR JOB — enumerate EVERY route handler in ALL ~45 route files and classify each param-taking data route as:\n- SAFE: scoped by ownerId/userId/patientIds in the where clause (name the file:line of the scoping)\n- VULNERABLE: fetches by bare id (prisma.X.findUnique({where:{id: req.params...}})) without ownership check → cross-tenant access to health data\n- UNCLEAR: needs dynamic check\nPay special attention to (user's stated focus): patient routes, exam routes (incl. file/photo serving), subscription/billing routes, and also sweep: items, analyses, chat, reminders, measurements, medications, vaccines, expenses, notifications, mental-screenings, risk, sports, achievements, tickets, devices, data (export!), doctor-share, doctor-question, doctor, labs, public-api v1.\n\nMETHOD: For each route file, map: route path → handler → prisma query where-clause → is req.userId (or derived patientIds) present? Use rg to find `findUnique`, `findFirst`, `update`, `delete` with `req.params` and check surrounding scope. The Exam→Patient→ownerId chain matters: a route scoped only by patientId WITHOUT verifying patient.ownerId===req.userId is vulnerable. Same for doctor-share tokens granting access to patient data.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n1. A prioritized candidate table (note titled 'bola-candidates', category findings): endpoint, file:line, missing check, object/impact (health data LGPD), confidence.\n2. record_coverage per route-file swept (surface = route file, risk = 'BOLA/object-level authorization') with outcome reported/ruled_out/needs_follow_up — be honest, name the control for ruled_out.\n3. Do NOT file vulnerability reports and do NOT run dynamic tests — discovery only. A validation agent will PoC the top candidates.",
