        "task": "Run the source-aware static triage bundle over /workspace/server (white-box scan; call get_threat_model target /workspace/server first for context).\n\nSHELL QUIRK: exec_command default pipes swallow output — always pass tty:true.\n\nRepo: /workspace/server (Express 5 + Prisma 6 + TypeScript). EXCLUDE node_modules and dist. Artifacts to /workspace/.source-aware/.\n\nDO ALL OF:\n1. semgrep scan --config p/default --config p/typescript --config p/secrets --metrics=off --json --output /workspace/.source-aware/semgrep.json /workspace/server/src\n2. Build sg-targets.txt from semgrep.json scope (paths.scanned, fallback unique results[].path), then xargs sg run --pattern '$F($$$ARGS)' --json=stream > /workspace/.source-aware/ast-grep.json (bounded to src/).\n3. gitleaks detect --source /workspace/server --report-format json --report-path /workspace/.source-aware/gitleaks.json (note: .env and janocaminho-*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json at repo root are KNOWN suspected secrets — include them but verify if they look real vs placeholders; also check git history if .git exists — it may be read-only, that's fine).\n4. trufflehog filesystem --no-update --json --no-verification /workspace/server > /workspace/.source-aware/trufflehog.json\n5. trivy fs --scanners vuln,misconfig --timeout 30m --offline-scan --format json --output /workspace/.source-aware/trivy-fs.json /workspace/server\n6. Summarize: top semgrep findings by severity with file:line; secret hits classified real-vs-placeholder (real secrets = finding candidates); dependency CVEs that are exploitable in this codebase (check reachability: is the vulnerable code path imported? e.g. sharp 0.32.6 used in middleware/upload or extraction).\n\nREPORTING RULES:\n- Do NOT file create_vulnerability_report — this is triage. Write a note (category general, title 'static-triage-results') with the prioritized candidate list incl. file:line.\n- For each REAL hardcoded secret (not placeholder), record_coverage with outcome 'needs_follow_up' listing it, evidence 'verified real secret at file:line' — a validation agent will confirm.\n- For each known-CVE dependency finding with a verified advisory + installed version in range, file it directly with create_dependency_report (that is allowed for you) — verify advisory CVSS via web_search first; set reachability honestly (check imports in src/).\nKeep artifacts bounded: trim ast-grep.json to src/ hits if huge.",
