        "task": "Set up the dynamic-validation harness for the Express+Prisma app at /workspace/server (threat model: get_threat_model target /workspace/server).\n\nGOAL: PostgreSQL test DB running on 127.0.0.1:5433 with database `meus_exames_test`, user `meus_exames` / password `meus_exames_dev`, schema migrated via prisma, and a green subset of the vitest suite.\n\nSTEPS:\n1. IMPORTANT SHELL QUIRK: exec_command with default (non-TTY) pipes SWALLOWS output in this sandbox — ALWAYS pass tty:true to exec_command to see output.\n2. Check if postgres is installed (which psql/initdb/pg_ctl). If not, install: `sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y postgresql postgresql-contrib` (or download binaries). Docker is NOT available.\n3. Initdb + start postgres on port 5433 (listen 127.0.0.1). Use a data dir under /tmp or /workspace/.pgdata. Create role meus_exames with password meus_exames_dev (SUPERUSER for test simplicity) and DB meus_exames_test owned by it.\n4. cd /workspace/server && DATABASE_URL='postgresql://meus_exames:meus_exames_dev@127.0.0.1:5433/meus_exames_test?schema=public' npx prisma migrate deploy (or `prisma db push` if migrations are out of sync).\n5. Verify: run one fast test file, e.g. `npx vitest run test/auth.test.ts` from /workspace/server. Then run test/billing.test.ts and test/asaas-webhook.test.ts to confirm billing tests pass.\n6. If some tests fail for environment reasons, note which pass/fail — do not fix app bugs.\n\nDELIVERABLE: leave postgres RUNNING (do not stop it). create_note (category methodology) titled 'test-harness' with: how to start postgres again if it dies, the DATABASE_URL to export, which vitest files pass, and any quirks. Then agent_finish with a summary. Record coverage for surface 'test harness' / risk 'dynamic validation infrastructure' with outcome no_issue_found/needs_follow_up as appropriate.",
