        "task": "Analyze billing webhook spoofing in /workspace/server (call get_threat_model target /workspace/server first).\n\nSHELL QUIRK: exec_command default pipes swallow output — always pass tty:true.\n\nKNOWN (from root): webhooks POST /api/webhooks/openpix and /api/webhooks/asaas are public, NOT HMAC-signed. Approval requires (1) pending Subscription with mpPaymentId == correlationID/payment.id, (2) amount match, (3) PENDING status. Billing routes RETURN paymentId (mpPaymentId) to the client (billing.routes.ts lines ~252/258/324/768/907). OpenPix correlationID format is `plan_<subId>`/`credits_<subId>_<n>`/`api_<subId>_<calls>`. OpenPix handler: if status empty → skips COMPLETED check; Asaas accepts event startsWith PAYMENT_RECEIVED or status in RECEIVED set.\n\nANALYZE (static, then dynamic when DB ready):\n1. Read src/routes/openpix-webhook.routes.ts, asaas-webhook.routes.ts, utils/billingApproval.ts, utils/subscriptionCompat.ts, routes/billing.routes.ts end-to-end. Confirm exact approval path and what a spoofed webhook grants (premium days? credits? API pack?). Check whether value must equal sub.amount exactly, and whether an attacker who OWNS a subscription (their own sub, PENDING) can approve it themselves via the public webhook with a crafted payload.\n2. Check GET /api/billing/... routes that expose paymentId/mpPaymentId to the subscribing user (lines ~895-907, 933-996 area) — attacker story: register → POST billing/pix-plan (creates PENDING sub) → read paymentId from response → POST /api/webhooks/openpix with {charge:{correlationID:paymentId,status:'COMPLETED'},payment:{value:amountCents}} → premium activated without payment. Verify EVERY step statically (exact response fields).\n3. Also check /billing/pay-card inline card path and any webhook-simulation endpoints (e.g. POST /billing/simulate or approval by paymentId lookup at line ~940 where userId IS checked — compare).\n4. Check jobs/pix-expiry.ts for race windows (approve vs expire).\n5. When the 'test-harness' note (see list_notes) says Postgres 5433 is up: build a dynamic PoC as a vitest file /workspace/server/test/poc-webhook-spoof.test.ts following test/asaas-webhook.test.ts patterns (resetDb, createUser, api() supertest). Prove premium/credits granted by crafted webhook POST with NO provider involvement. Run: cd /workspace/server && npx vitest run test/poc-webhook-spoof.test.ts. If harness not ready, deliver the static trace + mark dynamic as open gap.\n6. Counterevidence: look hard for any IP allowlist, secret header check, or provider verification we missed.\n\nDELIVERABLES: note 'webhook-spoof-analysis' (findings) with the full chain + file:line refs + PoC result. record_coverage (surface 'billing webhooks openpix+asaas', risk 'webhook spoofing'). Do NOT create_vulnerability_report — a reporting agent will file from your evidence.",
